course: dictionary
lesson: 9487
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Steamer is one of them: it can name a ship, a cooking pot, or a cleaning machine. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «The passing steamer made big waves on the river.» Waves and river show that a steamer is a boat. «Steam the carrots in a steamer.» Steam and carrots show that a steamer is a pot for cooking.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask what the sentence is about. Then try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
fact: Steamer means a ship or boat driven by a steam engine, also called a steamship.
fact: A steamer can also be a pan or pot with holes in it, which sits over boiling water to cook food in the steam.
fact: A steamer can be a machine that uses steam to clean things or take creases out of clothes.
fact: Steamers carried people across oceans and along rivers from the 1800s.
fact: Phrases such as «a paddle steamer» and «river steamer» mean a ship, while «steam vegetables in a steamer» means a cooking pot.
exercise: «The passing steamer made big waves on the river.» What is a steamer in this sentence? | A pan with holes for cooking | *A ship driven by a steam engine | A machine for ironing clothes | A kind of fish
exercise: Mum says, «Steam the carrots in a steamer.» What is a steamer here? | A river bank | *A pan with holes that sits over boiling water | A ship on the sea | A machine that takes creases out
exercise: Kipling writes of «the big steamers that sail weekly from Southampton». What does steamers mean in this sentence? | *Big ships that sail on the sea | Small wooden toys | Pans for cooking vegetables | Machines for ironing clothes
test: Dad uses a steamer to take the creases out of his shirt. What is a steamer here? | A large boat with sails | A ship on the river | *A machine that uses steam to take creases out | A pan for cooking rice
test: In «a paddle steamer» on the river, what does the word river tell you? | It shows the steamer is a fish | It shows the steamer is a pan for cooking | *It shows the steamer is a boat on water | It shows the steamer is a clothes machine
exam: Why must you read the words around steamer to know its meaning? | *Because steamer has several meanings, and the context shows which one | Because the dictionary is always wrong | Because steamer only ever means a ship | Because steamer is a very long word
